# Helios power-flow input for the GB network (AC part only).
#
# Solving this file reproduces the LFRESV records and transformer ratios in
# GBvoltrat.dat:
#
#   from stepss.helios import HeliosSession
#   pf = HeliosSession(); pf.load_file('GBpf.dat'); assert pf.solve()
#   pf.write_voltrat('GBpf_voltrat.dat'); pf.close()
#
# Helios has no HVDC model, so every converter appears as a constant P/Q load
# at its AC bus: Moyle 10 MW + 10 Mvar at bus 5, EWIC 500 MW at bus 12,
# HVDC2 at bus 26, and HVDC3 plus Nemo (1598 + 1000 MW) at bus 27.
# The interconnector-side buses (5IC, 12IC, 26IC, 27IC, 27IC2) and the DC buses
# are not in this file; their LFRESV records are set in GBdyn.dat/GBhvdc.txt.
#
# Loads, shunts and fixed SVC outputs are lumped into the BUS records, and each
# generator bus carries one aggregate GENER at its scheduled power. The 1510 MW
# exported over the three links is supplied by the non-nuclear, conventional-only
# stations (G17, G18, G21, G22, G25, G26, G28): each machine takes the same
# fraction (85.6%) of its headroom below its rated power Pnom. G26 is the slack.
# Buses with wind farms are limited to 0.44 pu of each farm's rating, divided
# by its active share, since every injector takes the same share of the bus
# reactive power as of its active power.
$SBASE 100. ;
$TOLAC 0.001 ;
$TOLREAC 0.001 ;
